  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Combined and Joint Variation 2 - Matatu fare</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A matatu owner shares the cost of a trip equally among the passengers. The cost per passenger, \(C\), varies directly with the distance travelled, \(d\), and inversely with the number of passengers, \(n\): \(C = \frac{kd}{n}\).</p>
<p>(a) On a trip of \({@pd1@}\) km with \({@pn1@}\) passengers, each passenger pays Ksh \({@pC1@}\). Find the value of \(k\).</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Use your value of \(k\) to find how much each passenger pays on a trip of \({@pd2@}\) km with \({@pn2@}\) passengers.</p>
<p>Cost per passenger = Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Substitute the first trip into \(C = \frac{kd}{n}\): \({@pC1@} = \frac{k({@pd1@})}{ {@pn1@} }\).</p>
<p>So \(k = \frac{ {@pC1@} \times {@pn1@} }{ {@pd1@} } = {@pk@}\).</p>
<p>Using \(C = \frac{ {@pk@}d}{n}\) with \(d = {@pd2@}\) and \(n = {@pn2@}\): \(C = \frac{ {@pk@}({@pd2@})}{ {@pn2@} } = {@pC2@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
